<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-dūro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. and n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make
			hard</i>, <i>to harden</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivem Indurat Boreas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 3, 9, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sues indurantes attritu arborum costas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 52, 78, § 212</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to harden</i>, <i>steel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indurandus est animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adversus omnia, quae accidere possunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontem,</span>”
				<i>to render shameless</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ben. 7, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to become hard</i>,
				<i>harden</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae (creta) si induraverit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. 3, 82, 2</span></i>
			.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indūrā-tus</span></b> , a, um,
				P. a., <i>hardened.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">robora indurata flammis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 64</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">induratus praeter spem resistendo hostium
					timor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					30, 18, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Germanis quid induratius ad omnem patientiam?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ira, 1, 11</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
